invariant: INV-14
file: srv_message.c
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: srv_certificate_fits admits a certificate of no bytes, which RFC
  9846 section 4.5.1 forbids (cert_data<1..2^24-1>), so a server sends a
  Certificate message every client refuses. bin/srv_quic_test requires
  ch_srv_quic_init to refuse an empty certificate with nothing sent.

--- old
        if (cert->der == NULL || cert->len == 0 || room < SRV_CERT_ENTRY_FRAME ||
--- new
        if (cert->der == NULL || room < SRV_CERT_ENTRY_FRAME ||
